    "perplexity": {
      "description": "In Concert/MTV Plugged captures Bruce Springsteen at a transitional moment in 1992, performing with his post-E Street Band and leaning into a harder, fully electric sound rather than the stripped-down approach MTV’s Unplugged format suggested. Recorded at Warner Hollywood Studios in Los Angeles and released by Columbia in 1993, it draws heavily on songs from Human Touch and Lucky Town while also revisiting earlier material such as “Atlantic City,” “Darkness on the Edge of Town,” and “Thunder Road.”\n\nThe album’s appeal lies in its raw, band-driven energy and its importance as an early live document of Springsteen’s 1990s era, when he was establishing a new identity outside the E Street Band. Reception has often focused on the strength of performances like “Better Days,” “If I Should Fall Behind,” and “Living Proof,” with the set also notable for featuring first recorded appearances of “Light of Day” and “Red Headed Woman.”",
